  (text "SW1 can sit on the board or be wired\nto an external 6 mm button." (at 180.34 134.62 0)
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 5ed5b10a-9691-5e0a-8bf2-6494d9fb35a9)
  )
  (text "MPU-6050 I2C address 0x68\n(AD0 pulled low on the GY-521)" (at 160.02 106.68 0)
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 12a4e911-0fb0-5562-987f-a3cacbcf0b32)
  )
  (text "NOTES\n1. Same connections as the kit's point-to-point wiring diagram:\n   D5 (GPIO5) -> LED panel DIN, D4 (GPIO4) -> button to GND,\n   D21/D22 -> MPU-6050 SDA/SCL, 3V3 -> MPU-6050 VCC.\n2. The 4xAA pack (J1, has its own switch) feeds the LED panel's extra red/white\n   power wires (J2) directly; the ESP32 runs from the same rail through VIN and\n   its on-board 3.3 V regulator.\n3. U1 accepts 30-pin ESP32 DevKit boards with 0.9 in (22.86 mm) or\n   1.0 in (25.4 mm) header spacing: header 1 has both rows of holes.\n4. J1-J3 accept 3.5 mm screw terminals or wires soldered straight in." (at 25.4 142.24 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 821eb0e1-c81a-58d2-abcc-2ad4e2b3fc4c)
  )
